// How long a block takes to break (pbd_core::dig), in seconds. The right
// tool breaks a material in its base time: the shovel soft ground (grass,
// soil, dirt, sand, snow), the pickaxe stone, rock and ore. Any other tool
// takes wrong_tool times as long, and the rod breaks nothing. A torch breaks
// at placed_s with any tool. With the button held, the next block starts
// between_s after the last one broke.
//
// The code defaults written out; a test holds the two together. Why these
// numbers: openspec/changes/fishing-and-equipment/design.md section 3.
(
    soft_s: 0.5,
    stone_s: 1.2,
    rock_s: 1.6,
    ore_s: 2.0,
    placed_s: 0.1,
    wrong_tool: 4.0,
    between_s: 0.15,
)
